Resolutions
12. Consideration of a resolution approving 307 Horse Racing, Inc,  to
conduct parimutuel wagering on live horse racing, historic horse
racing and simulcast events at 3310 Ridge Rd, Cheyenne, Laramie
County, WY.
24 - 198
Resolution, 307 Horse Racing, Inc, Parimutuel
Wagering
Attachments:
Mark Voss, County Attorney, explained the purpose of the resolution is to add another
location in Laramie County, and the board of county commissioners will have more
oversight over the operation.
Chairman Lovett opened the meeting for PUBLIC COMMENT. Kyle Ridgeway,
applicant, noted the services provided by the Pershing Blvd facility and said there is a
need for a second facility to meet increasing demand. Ridgeway said the resolution
provides more local control in terms of reporting, monitoring, the ability to revoke, and
time periods for renewal. Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Lovett
closed the comment period.
Commissioner Thompson expressed his appreciation for 307 Horse Racing's
proactive approach and resolution for additional local control.
A motion was made by Commissioner Thompson, seconded by Vice
Chairman Malm, that this agenda item be approved. The motion carried by
