Items #15, #18, #19 and #20 were consolidated into one public hearing and motion
with separate votes.
15. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a seasonal fireworks permit submitted
by Breanna Elliott, dba Jurassic Fireworks, located at 201 I-25
Service Rd Bldg A.
24 - 181
Permit, Jurassic Fireworks, 201 I-25 Service Rd Bldg A
Attachments:
Dale Davis, County Clerk Chief Deputy, said the applications were in order, and Matt
Butler, Fire Warden, said the inspections were completed.
Chairman Lovett opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Hearing no PUBLIC
COMMENT, Chairman Lovett closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Malm, seconded by Commissioner
Thompson, that this agenda item be approved.
Commissioner Thompson talked about how the applicant had previously treated
county staff. He referenced complaints received last summer from surrounding
businesses about the applicant's behavior disrupting other businesses.
Commissioner Thompson stated he was not in favor of the applicant receiving a
permit. Commissioner Holmes expressed the same concerns and noted the multiple
times the sheriff was called to the area.
The motion failed by the following vote:
Lovett
Aye:
Malm, Heath, Holmes, Thompson
Nay:
