### Page 9 of 10

```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
April 16, 2024
Commissioner Malm asked about the screening area on the site plan along
Highland Dr. Suzy Troncin and Shaw Teasley, applicants, said there is existing
shrubbery.
Arnold said based on evidence provided, staff recommends approval with the
adoption of findings of fact a and b with the following condition: Per the
Cheyenne/Laramie County Environmental Health Division, the septic system shall be
engineered for the site prior to the issuance of a Certificate of Review.
Chairman Lovett opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Steve Harrington,
resident, welcomed the business and thanked the county for the road work. Hearing
no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Lovett closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Commissioner Holmes, seconded by
Commissioner Thompson, to approve the site plan with one condition and
adopt findings of fact a and b of the staff report.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Malm, seconded by Commissioner
Thompson, to amend the motion to include that the applicant will obtain an
access permit from Laramie County Public Works after the road is done.
The motion carried by the following vote:
Lovett, Malm, Heath, Holmes, Thompson
Aye:
The board asked Teasley if he was agreeable to the additional condition. Teasley
acknowledged his agreement with the amendment.
The motion as amended carried by the following vote:
Lovett, Malm, Heath, Holmes, Thompson
Aye:
24. PUBLIC HEARING regarding approval for a vacation of Lots 3 and 4,
Block 1, Apple Valley, a parcel in the SW1/4 of the NE1/4 of Sect 18,
T13N, R66W, and approval of an administrative plat, Apple Valley,
2nd Filing, Laramie County, WY.
